#
# Counter-example for math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentDisjointShape (Rule P11): a node typed
# BOTH math:ProbabilityEvent (a measurable set of outcomes) AND logic:Event (an occurrent
# that happens in time). The two are held owl:disjointWith, so the sh:not [ sh:class
# logic:Event ] fires — shacl.NotConstraintComponent (math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentConflation).
# Single violation: the node carries neither math:hasElement nor math:memberCondition, so the
# inherited math:Set extent SPARQL gate stays SILENT — EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling fires.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityEvent owl:disjointWith logic:Event / math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityEventOccurrentConflationBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:conflatedRain a math:ProbabilityEvent , logic:Event .
